    <main style="padding-top:56px;">

        <section style="padding:1.5rem 0 0.5rem 0; border-bottom: none;">
            <div class="page-col">
                <div style="background: rgba(16,185,129,0.08); border: 2px solid var(--green); border-radius: var(--card-r); padding: 1.5rem 1.8rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                    <h3 style="color: var(--green); font-size: 1rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem;">
                        <i class="fas fa-laptop-code"></i> Run This Page Locally – Python Setup Instructions
                    </h3>
                    <p style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text); line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 0.8rem;">
                        This page is designed as a <strong>reference and learning resource</strong>.
                        The <strong>"Run"</strong> button uses <strong>Pyodide</strong> (Python in your browser)
                        and can only execute pure Python code.
                        <strong style="color: var(--gold);">For the advanced automation examples</strong>
                        (Selenium, OpenCV, psutil, watchdog, etc.), you <strong>must run them locally</strong>
                        on your own computer.
                    </p>
                    <div style="background: var(--code-bg); border-radius: var(--btn-r); padding: 1rem 1.2rem; margin: 0.8rem 0; border: 1px solid var(--border);">
                        <p style="font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--blue-lt); margin-bottom: 0.3rem; font-weight: 700;">
                            <i class="fas fa-terminal"></i> Step 1: Install Python dependencies
                        </p>
