        <section id="os-path" aria-labelledby="os-heading">
            <div class="page-col">
                <div class="section-intro">
                    <h2 id="os-heading">📂 Working with Paths — <code>os</code> and <code>pathlib</code></h2>
                    <p>Every automation script starts with navigating the filesystem. Learn the modern way with <code>pathlib</code>.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="oop-block">
                    <h3>📂 1.1 <code>pathlib</code> — Object‑Oriented Paths</h3>
                    <p><code>pathlib</code> provides an object‑oriented interface to filesystem paths. It''s cleaner, more readable, and cross‑platform.</p>

                    <h4 style="color:var(--blue-lt);font-size:0.8rem;margin-top:0.8rem;margin-bottom:0.4rem;">Step-by-step explanation:</h4>
                    <ul class="step-list">
                        <li><strong>Step 1:</strong> Import <code>Path</code> from <code>pathlib</code>.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 2:</strong> Create a <code>Path</code> object pointing to the current directory using <code>Path.cwd()</code>.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 3:</strong> Use <code>path.exists()</code>, <code>path.is_dir()</code>, and <code>path.is_file()</code> to check properties.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 4:</strong> List all files in the current directory using <code>path.iterdir()</code>.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 5:</strong> Use <code>path / "subfolder" / "file.txt"</code> to build paths — the <code>/</code> operator is overloaded.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 6:</strong> Access the parent directory with <code>.parent</code>, file name with <code>.name</code>, and extension with <code>.suffix</code>.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <div class="code-container" data-code=''from pathlib import Path

def pathlib_demo():
    # Current working directory
    cwd = Path.cwd()
    print(f"Current directory: {cwd}")

    # Check properties
    print(f"Exists: {cwd.exists()}")
    print(f"Is directory: {cwd.is_dir()}")

    # List contents
    print("\nContents:")
    for item in cwd.iterdir():
        print(f"  {item.name} ({&#39;dir&#39; if item.is_dir() else &#39;file&#39;})")

    # Build paths
    sub = cwd / "data" / "config.json"
    print(f"\nBuilt path: {sub}")
    print(f"Parent: {sub.parent}")
    print(f"Name: {sub.name}")
    print(f"Suffix: {sub.suffix}")

pathlib_demo()''>
                        <div class="code-header">
                            <span style="color:var(--muted);">python</span>
                            <div class="code-actions">
                                <button class="code-btn copy-btn"><i class="fas fa-copy"></i> Copy</button>
                                <button class="code-btn run-btn"><i class="fas fa-play"></i> Run</button>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="code-snippet"><pre><span class="kw">from</span> pathlib <span class="kw">import</span> Path

<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">pathlib_demo</span>():
    cwd = Path.cwd()
    <span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"Current directory: {cwd}"</span>)

    <span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"Exists: {cwd.exists()}"</span>)
    <span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"Is directory: {cwd.is_dir()}"</span>)

    <span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">"\nContents:"</span>)
    <span class="kw">for</span> item <span class="kw">in</span> cwd.iterdir():
        <span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"  {item.name} ({''dir'' if item.is_dir() else ''file''})"</span>)

    sub = cwd / <span class="st">"data"</span> / <span class="st">"config.json"</span>
    <span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"\nBuilt path: {sub}"</span>)
    <span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"Parent: {sub.parent}"</span>)
    <span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"Name: {sub.name}"</span>)
    <span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"Suffix: {sub.suffix}"</span>)

pathlib_demo()</pre></div>
                        <div class="output-panel"></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="insight">💡 <code>pathlib</code> handles path separators automatically — your code works on Windows, macOS, and Linux without modification.</div>
                </div>

                <div class="oop-block">
                    <h3>📂 1.2 <code>os</code> Module — Traditional Path Operations</h3>
                    <p>The <code>os</code> module provides low‑level system functions. Still widely used in legacy code and for operations not yet in <code>pathlib</code>.</p>

                    <h4 style="color:var(--blue-lt);font-size:0.8rem;margin-top:0.8rem;margin-bottom:0.4rem;">Step-by-step explanation:</h4>
                    <ul class="step-list">
                        <li><strong>Step 1:</strong> Import <code>os</code> — the standard library for operating system interfaces.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 2:</strong> Use <code>os.getcwd()</code> to get the current working directory (string).</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 3:</strong> Use <code>os.listdir()</code> to list files in a directory.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 4:</strong> Use <code>os.path.join()</code> to build paths — this is cross‑platform.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 5:</strong> Use <code>os.path.exists()</code>, <code>os.path.isdir()</code>, and <code>os.path.isfile()</code> to check properties.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 6:</strong> Use <code>os.environ</code> to access environment variables — useful for configuration.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <div class="code-container" data-code=''import os

def os_demo():
    cwd = os.getcwd()
    print(f"Current directory: {cwd}")

    print("\nFiles (os.listdir):")
    for name in os.listdir(cwd):
        path = os.path.join(cwd, name)
        if os.path.isdir(path):
            print(f"  📁 {name}")
        else:
            print(f"  📄 {name}")

    config_path = os.path.join(cwd, "config", "settings.ini")
    print(f"\nBuilt path: {config_path}")
    print(f"Exists: {os.path.exists(config_path)}")

    print("\nEnvironment variables (first 3):")
    env = os.environ
    for i, (k, v) in enumerate(env.items()):
        if i >= 3: break
        print(f"  {k}={v[:30]}...")

os_demo()''>
