                <div class="oop-block">
                    <h3>📄 2.2 Working with Directories</h3>
                    <p>Create, rename, list, and delete directories — essential for any automation script.</p>

                    <h4 style="color:var(--blue-lt);font-size:0.8rem;margin-top:0.8rem;margin-bottom:0.4rem;">Step-by-step explanation:</h4>
                    <ul class="step-list">
                        <li><strong>Step 1:</strong> Create a directory with <code>Path.mkdir()</code>.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 2:</strong> Check if a directory exists with <code>Path.exists()</code>.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 3:</strong> Create nested directories with <code>parents=True</code>.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 4:</strong> List directory contents with <code>iterdir()</code>.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 5:</strong> Remove an empty directory with <code>Path.rmdir()</code>.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 6:</strong> Remove a directory and all its contents with <code>shutil.rmtree()</code>.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <div class="code-container" data-code=''from pathlib import Path
import shutil

def dir_demo():
    base = Path.cwd() / "automation_test"
    nested = base / "sub" / "subsub"

    # Create directories
    nested.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    print(f"✅ Created: {nested}")

    # Create a file inside
    (base / "sub" / "hello.txt").write_text("Hello nested dir!")

    # List recursively
    print("\n📂 Directory tree:")
    for item in base.rglob("*"):
        indent = "  " * (len(item.relative_to(base).parts) - 1)
        print(f"{indent}📄 {item.name}" if item.is_file() else f"{indent}📁 {item.name}")

    # Clean up
    shutil.rmtree(base, ignore_errors=True)
    print(f"\n🧹 Deleted: {base}")

dir_demo()''>
