                <div class="oop-block">
                    <h3>📦 3.2 Archiving — ZIP and TAR</h3>
                    <p>Create and extract archives programmatically — perfect for backups and distribution.</p>

                    <h4 style="color:var(--blue-lt);font-size:0.8rem;margin-top:0.8rem;margin-bottom:0.4rem;">Step-by-step explanation:</h4>
                    <ul class="step-list">
                        <li><strong>Step 1:</strong> Create a directory with some files to archive.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 2:</strong> Use <code>shutil.make_archive()</code> to create a ZIP archive.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 3:</strong> Use <code>shutil.unpack_archive()</code> to extract the archive.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 4:</strong> List the contents of the extracted directory.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 5:</strong> Clean up the temporary files.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <div class="code-container" data-code=''from pathlib import Path
import shutil

def archive_demo():
    base = Path.cwd() / "archive_test"
    base.mkdir(exist_ok=True)

    # Create files
    (base / "file1.txt").write_text("Content 1")
    (base / "file2.txt").write_text("Content 2")
    sub = base / "sub"
    sub.mkdir()
    (sub / "file3.txt").write_text("Content 3")

    # Create archive
    archive_name = shutil.make_archive("my_archive", "zip", base)
    print(f"✅ Created archive: {archive_name}")

    # Extract
    extract_dir = Path.cwd() / "extracted"
    shutil.unpack_archive(archive_name, extract_dir)
    print(f"✅ Extracted to: {extract_dir}")

    # List extracted
    print("\n📂 Extracted contents:")
    for item in extract_dir.rglob("*"):
        if item.is_file():
            print(f"  📄 {item.relative_to(extract_dir)}")

    # Clean up
    shutil.rmtree(base, ignore_errors=True)
    shutil.rmtree(extract_dir, ignore_errors=True)
    Path(archive_name).unlink(missing_ok=True)
    print("\n🧹 Cleaned up")

archive_demo()''>
