                <div class="oop-block">
                    <h3>💻 4.2 Piping and Advanced Control</h3>
                    <p>Chain commands, set environment variables, and control timeouts.</p>

                    <h4 style="color:var(--blue-lt);font-size:0.8rem;margin-top:0.8rem;margin-bottom:0.4rem;">Step-by-step explanation:</h4>
                    <ul class="step-list">
                        <li><strong>Step 1:</strong> Use <code>subprocess.Popen()</code> for more control.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 2:</strong> Pipe output from one command to another.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 3:</strong> Set environment variables with the <code>env</code> parameter.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 4:</strong> Set a timeout to prevent hanging.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 5:</strong> Handle the timeout exception.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <div class="code-container" data-code=''import subprocess
import os

def advanced_subprocess():
    # Pipe: ls | grep .py
    p1 = subprocess.Popen(["ls"], stdout=subprocess.PIPE, text=True)
    p2 = subprocess.Popen(["grep", ".py"], stdin=p1.stdout, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, text=True)
    p1.stdout.close()
    output = p2.communicate()[0]
    print("🔍 Python files:")
    print(output)

    # Custom environment
    env = os.environ.copy()
    env["MY_VAR"] = "automation"
    result = subprocess.run(["printenv", "MY_VAR"], env=env, capture_output=True, text=True)
    print(f"✅ MY_VAR = {result.stdout.strip()}")

advanced_subprocess()''>
