                <div class="oop-block">
                    <h3>⏰ 5.2 Cron‑Like Scheduling with <code>apscheduler</code></h3>
                    <p><code>apscheduler</code> provides cron‑like scheduling with more advanced features.</p>

                    <h4 style="color:var(--blue-lt);font-size:0.8rem;margin-top:0.8rem;margin-bottom:0.4rem;">Step-by-step explanation:</h4>
                    <ul class="step-list">
                        <li><strong>Step 1:</strong> Import <code>BackgroundScheduler</code> from <code>apscheduler.schedulers.background</code>.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 2:</strong> Import <code>CronTrigger</code> for cron‑style scheduling.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 3:</strong> Define a function to run on schedule.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 4:</strong> Create a <code>BackgroundScheduler</code> and add a job.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 5:</strong> Start the scheduler.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 6:</strong> Keep the program running for a few seconds.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 7:</strong> Shut down the scheduler.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <div class="code-container" data-code=''from apscheduler.schedulers.background import BackgroundScheduler
from apscheduler.triggers.cron import CronTrigger
import time

def cron_task():
    print(f"⏰ Cron task ran at {time.strftime(&#39;%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S&#39;)}")

def cron_demo():
    scheduler = BackgroundScheduler()
    # Run every 2 seconds (cron-style)
    scheduler.add_job(cron_task, CronTrigger(second="*/2"))
    scheduler.start()
    print("⏳ Cron scheduler running for 6 seconds...")

    time.sleep(6)
    scheduler.shutdown()
    print("✅ Cron scheduler stopped")

cron_demo()''>
                        <div class="code-header">
                            <span style="color:var(--muted);">python</span>
