                <div class="oop-block">
                    <h3>📧 7.1 Sending Email with <code>smtplib</code></h3>
                    <p>Use <code>smtplib</code> to send emails via SMTP servers.</p>

                    <h4 style="color:var(--blue-lt);font-size:0.8rem;margin-top:0.8rem;margin-bottom:0.4rem;">Step-by-step explanation:</h4>
                    <ul class="step-list">
                        <li><strong>Step 1:</strong> Import <code>smtplib</code> and <code>email.message</code>.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 2:</strong> Create an <code>EmailMessage</code> object.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 3:</strong> Set <code>From</code>, <code>To</code>, <code>Subject</code>, and body.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 4:</strong> Connect to an SMTP server using <code>smtplib.SMTP()</code>.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 5:</strong> Start TLS with <code>starttls()</code> for security.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 6:</strong> Log in and send the email.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 7:</strong> Quit the connection.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <div class="code-container" data-code=''import smtplib
from email.message import EmailMessage

def email_demo():
    msg = EmailMessage()
    msg["From"] = "automation@example.com"
    msg["To"] = "recipient@example.com"
    msg["Subject"] = "Automation Report"
    msg.set_content("This is an automated email from Python.")

    print("📧 Email built:")
    print(f"  From: {msg[&#39;From&#39;]}")
    print(f"  To: {msg[&#39;To&#39;]}")
    print(f"  Subject: {msg[&#39;Subject&#39;]}")
    print(f"  Body: {msg.get_content()}")

    print("\n💡 In production, connect to an SMTP server with:")
    print("  server = smtplib.SMTP(''smtp.example.com'', 587)")
    print("  server.starttls()")
    print("  server.login(''user'', ''password'')")
    print("  server.send_message(msg)")
    print("  server.quit()")

email_demo()''>
