            <div class="page-col">
                <div class="section-intro">
                    <h2 id="excel-heading">📊 Excel Automation — <code>openpyxl</code></h2>
                    <p>Read, write, and manipulate Excel files with <code>openpyxl</code> — no Excel needed.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="oop-block">
                    <h3>📊 8.1 Reading and Writing Excel Files</h3>
                    <p>Use <code>openpyxl</code> to work with <code>.xlsx</code> files programmatically.</p>

                    <h4 style="color:var(--blue-lt);font-size:0.8rem;margin-top:0.8rem;margin-bottom:0.4rem;">Step-by-step explanation:</h4>
                    <ul class="step-list">
                        <li><strong>Step 1:</strong> Import <code>openpyxl</code> and <code>Path</code>.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 2:</strong> Create a new workbook with <code>Workbook()</code>.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 3:</strong> Select the active sheet or create a new one.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 4:</strong> Write data to cells using <code>sheet["A1"] = "value"</code>.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 5:</strong> Save the workbook with <code>wb.save()</code>.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 6:</strong> Load an existing workbook with <code>load_workbook()</code>.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 7:</strong> Iterate over rows and cells to read data.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <div class="code-container" data-code=''from openpyxl import Workbook, load_workbook
from pathlib import Path

def excel_demo():
    filename = "automation.xlsx"
    path = Path(filename)

    # Create and write
    wb = Workbook()
    ws = wb.active
    ws.title = "Data"

    ws["A1"] = "Name"
    ws["B1"] = "Score"
    ws.append(["Alice", 95])
    ws.append(["Bob", 88])
    ws.append(["Charlie", 92])

    wb.save(filename)
    print(f"✅ Created {filename}")

    # Read
    wb = load_workbook(filename)
    ws = wb["Data"]

    print("\n📊 Data:")
    for row in ws.iter_rows(values_only=True):
        print(f"  {row}")

    # Clean up
    path.unlink(missing_ok=True)
    print("\n🧹 Deleted file")

excel_demo()''>
