                <div class="oop-block">
                    <h3>🚀 11.1 Backup Script</h3>
                    <p>A complete backup script that creates timestamped archives of a directory.</p>

                    <h4 style="color:var(--blue-lt);font-size:0.8rem;margin-top:0.8rem;margin-bottom:0.4rem;">Step-by-step explanation:</h4>
                    <ul class="step-list">
                        <li><strong>Step 1:</strong> Import <code>shutil</code>, <code>pathlib</code>, and <code>datetime</code>.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 2:</strong> Define source and backup directories.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 3:</strong> Generate a timestamp for the archive name.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 4:</strong> Use <code>shutil.make_archive()</code> to create the backup.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step 5:</strong> Print success message with the backup location.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <div class="code-container" data-code=''from pathlib import Path
import shutil
from datetime import datetime

def backup_demo():
    source = Path.cwd() / "data_to_backup"
    source.mkdir(exist_ok=True)

    # Create some dummy files
    (source / "file1.txt").write_text("Backup this!")
    (source / "file2.txt").write_text("And this too!")

    backup_dir = Path.cwd() / "backups"
    backup_dir.mkdir(exist_ok=True)

    timestamp = datetime.now().strftime("%Y%m%d_%H%M%S")
    archive_name = backup_dir / f"backup_{timestamp}"

    shutil.make_archive(str(archive_name), "zip", source)
    print(f"✅ Backup created: {archive_name}.zip")

    # Clean up
    shutil.rmtree(source, ignore_errors=True)
    Path(f"{archive_name}.zip").unlink(missing_ok=True)
    backup_dir.rmdir()
    print("🧹 Cleaned up")

backup_demo()''>
